KV v2 has three delete levels: soft (DELETE data/:path, POST delete/:path), destroy a version (PUT destroy/:path), and key+all-versions (DELETE metadata/:path). delete_secret implements only level 3, the irreversible one, under a name that reads like level 1. Add the soft delete / undelete / destroy methods, and make the POD state which level each performs.

2026-09-09 07:07 Done. Added reversible delete-ladder methods soft_delete_secret (level 1 reversible), undelete_secret (restore), destroy_secret (level 2 irreversible per version). delete_secret unchanged (level 3, irreversible, metadata). POD now states each level and reversibility with cross-links; data-loss of destroy and delete_secret called out. New path helpers plus offline test 40-delete-ladder.t (verb, path, versions body, delete_secret contract guard, croak-before-seam, custom mount) and helper assertions in 10-paths.t. prove -lr t green with 45 tests, dzil test PASS. Commit 065a383.
